 "briefing": {
  "historical": "On 18 November 1941 the British Eighth Army launched Operation Crusader to relieve the besieged fortress of Tobruk and retake Cyrenaica from Panzergruppe Afrika (N02). Tank battles around Sidi Rezegh, Rommel's dash to the wire and a severe Axis fuel shortage ended with the Axis retreat to El Agheila by late December.",
  "situation": "The Allies must break the Axis ring around Tobruk and destroy the Afrika Korps; the Axis must hold the Tobruk siege, protect the frontier garrisons and their thin, fuel-starved supply line. Start positions are approximate sector anchors."
 },
